# Day 2 — Docker Images

## What is a Docker Image?

A Docker image is a read-only template containing the files,
dependencies, configuration, and metadata required to create
a container.

## Image → Container

Image
↓
docker run
↓
Container

## Image Reference

A Docker image can be referenced as:

REGISTRY/NAMESPACE/REPOSITORY:TAG

Example:

docker.io/library/ubuntu:24.04

## Important Commands

```bash
docker pull ubuntu:24.04
docker image ls
docker image inspect ubuntu:24.04
docker image history ubuntu:24.04
docker image tag ubuntu:24.04 my-ubuntu:v1
docker image rm IMAGE
